# Week 1 — Initial Discovery 

## 1. Facts 
Record at least 5 things that we know from the scenario. 
1. The college is considering a college equipment booking system.
2. This will be for shared equipment such as laptops, camera, projectors and specialist equipment.
3. Bookings are currently being managed using a mixture of email, spreadsheets and informal arrangements.
4. Currently the equipment can be double-booked.
5. People are sometimes unsure whether equipment is available.
6. Staff must spend time checking the bookings manually.
7. The equipment may not be returned when it is expected.
8. Students are not always sure on who they need to contact about booking the equipment.

## 2. Assumptions 
Record at least 4 things you are currently assuming but have not been told.
1. That some staff memembers are also unsure who they need to contact about booking the equipment.
2. That people who are booking the equipment are unsure of or forgetting the return deadline.
3. That not all bookings are being recorded properly.
4. That some people are not aware that booking this equipment is something they can do.

## 3. Unknowns 
Record at least 4 important things we do not yet know.
1. How bookings are currently being cancelled.
2. Is there diffent amounts of time each piece of equipment can be booked.
3. The amount of each piece of equipment that is available to be booked.
4. If there is a current queue/wait times for any of the equipment
5. How can bookings be cancelled.
6. If bookings can be extended.
7. Who is allowed to book specialist equipment.
8. What happens if equipment is returned late.
9. What information is required to create a booking.

## 4. Stakeholders 
Identify at least 5 stakeholders. 
1. Students.
2. Lecturers.
3. Equipment Technician.
4. Equipment Manager.
5. Department Administrator.
6. IT Staff.
7. Requirements Engineer.

## 5. Goals 
Identify 3 goals for the proposed system.
1. The system should help the college to see which equipment is currently available and unavailable.
2. The system should help the college to advise students on how long they may borrow the equipment for.
3. The system should help the college to send out reminders on bookings.

